    "id": 899379,
    "name": "Honey Crisp Apple (WA)",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Honeycrisp apples are medium to large, round or oblate apples with a yellow-green background and a red-orange flush. Their skin can be mottled red, with shallow dimples and small dots, and sometimes russeting at the stem end. The flesh is white or ivory, crisp, and aromatic. Honeycrisp apples have a sweet-tart flavor that can be mild if harvested early or if the trees are heavily cropped. They are known for their exceptional juiciness and crunch, which some say is like biting into a ripe peach.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Grown by: </span><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=Joyfully+Grown+apples&amp;rlz=1CAVNCX_enUS1049US1049&amp;oq=where+is+joyfully+grown+&amp;gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUqCAgBEAAYFhgeMgYIABBFGDkyCAgBEAAYFhgeMg0IAhAAGIYDGIAEGIoFMg0IAxAAGIYDGIAEGIoFMg0IBBAAGIYDGIAEGIoFMgoIBRAAGKIEGIkFMgoIBhAAGIAEGKIEMgcIBxAAGO8FMgcICBAAGO8F0gEKMTA3MzBqMGoxNagCCLACAfEF-lV8BgjUFhrxBfpVfAYI1BYa&amp;sourceid=chrome&amp;ie=UTF-8&amp;mstk=AUtExfAeaGrh6zaQh68eMhQrFZ0G-3Xsqvb1_pDOWJl0y8Z82O2SEpsPpqvMeAzDa2jLbQDvmpTwTu8Tvi4d6rCbpqHYiB34S2TNwfhGPx0wjfYLC40HBnCXpQLKGmF-N03oJ7liVClH7KwgfUGXAVUlJiCGlIgtvUUNMOPNib5XUutA2pE&amp;csui=3&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiYvt3uvOGTAxX9weYEHbK7K-IQgK4QegQIARAB\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Joyfully Grown apples</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">&nbsp;are certified organic, premium fruit grown in&nbsp;the&nbsp;</span><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">foothills of the Cascade Mountain range in North Central Washington State</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">. Produced by&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://chelanfresh.com/joyfully-grown-organic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"lexical-text-editor--link\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Chelan Fresh</span></a><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">, these apples are handpicked on family farms that have been operating in Washington since 1894.</span></p>",
